## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model regulatory data residency in a managed RDBMS with cross-region replication, plus practical routing, isolation, backup and DR testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Data residency routing and tenant isolation
- Aurora Global Database writer/read topology
- Per-tenant schemas vs. separate databases
- IAM, KMS, backups, DR drills, latency validation

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-router: selects region, endpoints, and access controls per-tenant
function routeRequest(tenantId, operation) {
  const region = residencyMap[tenantId];
  const writer = regionWriterEndpoint[region];
  const readers = regionReadEndpoints[region];
  return { writer, readers, region };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle a tenant migration from one residency region to another?
- What monitoring would you implement to detect cross-region lag impacting reads?
